> nthroots 2 -1
the 2 square roots of -1 (w^2 = -1)
  w0 = i                      = e^(i*pi/2)  (principal)
  w1 = -i                     = e^(-i*pi/2)
  check: each w^2, parsed back as printed, equals -1 numerically
> nthroots 3 -1
the 3 cube roots of -1 (w^3 = -1)
  w0 = 1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(i*pi/3)  (principal)
  w1 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)
  w2 = 1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(-i*pi/3)
  check: each w^3, parsed back as printed, equals -1 numerically
> nthroots 4 -1
the 4 fourth roots of -1 (w^4 = -1)
  w0 = sqrt(2)/2 + i*sqrt(2)/2 = e^(i*pi/4)  (principal)
  w1 = -sqrt(2)/2 + i*sqrt(2)/2 = e^(i*3pi/4)
  w2 = -sqrt(2)/2 - i*sqrt(2)/2 = e^(-i*3pi/4)
  w3 = sqrt(2)/2 - i*sqrt(2)/2 = e^(-i*pi/4)
  check: each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals -1 numerically
> nthroots 2 i
the 2 square roots of i (w^2 = i)
  w0 = sqrt(2)/2 + i*sqrt(2)/2 = e^(i*pi/4)  (principal)
  w1 = -sqrt(2)/2 - i*sqrt(2)/2 = e^(-i*3pi/4)
  check: each w^2, parsed back as printed, equals i numerically
> nthroots 3 8
the 3 cube roots of 8 (w^3 = 8)
  w0 = 2                      = 2  (principal)
  w1 = -1 + i*sqrt(3)         = 2*e^(i*2pi/3)
  w2 = -1 - i*sqrt(3)         = 2*e^(-i*2pi/3)
  check: each w^3, parsed back as printed, equals 8 numerically
> nthroots 3 -8
the 3 cube roots of -8 (w^3 = -8)
  w0 = 1 + i*sqrt(3)          = 2*e^(i*pi/3)  (principal)
  w1 = -2                     = 2*e^(i*pi)
  w2 = 1 - i*sqrt(3)          = 2*e^(-i*pi/3)
  check: each w^3, parsed back as printed, equals -8 numerically
> unity 4
the 4 fourth roots of 1 (w^4 = 1)
  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)
  w1 = i                      = e^(i*pi/2)
  w2 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)
  w3 = -i                     = e^(-i*pi/2)
  check: each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically
> unity 3
the 3 cube roots of 1 (w^3 = 1)
  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)
  w1 = -1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2     = e^(i*2pi/3)
  w2 = -1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2     = e^(-i*2pi/3)
  check: each w^3, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically
> unity 6
the 6 sixth roots of 1 (w^6 = 1)
  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)
  w1 = 1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(i*pi/3)
  w2 = -1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2     = e^(i*2pi/3)
  w3 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)
  w4 = -1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2     = e^(-i*2pi/3)
  w5 = 1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(-i*pi/3)
  check: each w^6, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically
> complex (-1)^(1/2)
(-1)^(1/2) = i
  Re = 0,  Im = 1
  check: equal numerically (1i, complex arithmetic)
> complex (-1)^(1/3)
(-1)^(1/3) = 1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2
  Re = 1/2,  Im = sqrt(3)/2
  check: equal numerically (0.5 + 0.8660254038i, complex arithmetic)
> complex (-1)^(2/3)
(-1)^(2/3) = -1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2
  Re = -1/2,  Im = sqrt(3)/2
  check: equal numerically (-0.5 + 0.8660254038i, complex arithmetic)
> complex (-1)^(1/4)
(-1)^(1/4) = sqrt(2)/2 + i*sqrt(2)/2
  Re = sqrt(2)/2,  Im = sqrt(2)/2
  check: equal numerically (0.7071067812 + 0.7071067812i, complex arithmetic)
> complex (-1)^(3/4)
(-1)^(3/4) = -sqrt(2)/2 + i*sqrt(2)/2
  Re = -sqrt(2)/2,  Im = sqrt(2)/2
  check: equal numerically (-0.7071067812 + 0.7071067812i, complex arithmetic)
> complex (-8)^(1/3)
(-8)^(1/3) = 1 + i*sqrt(3)
  Re = 1,  Im = sqrt(3)
  check: equal numerically (1 + 1.732050808i, complex arithmetic)
> complex i^(1/2)
i^(1/2) = sqrt(2)/2 + i*sqrt(2)/2
  Re = sqrt(2)/2,  Im = sqrt(2)/2
  check: equal numerically (0.7071067812 + 0.7071067812i, complex arithmetic)
> complex (1+i)^(1/2)
(1+i)^(1/2) = sqrt((1 + sqrt(2))/2) + i*sqrt((-1 + sqrt(2))/2)
  Re = sqrt((1 + sqrt(2))/2),  Im = sqrt((-1 + sqrt(2))/2)
  check: equal numerically (1.098684113 + 0.4550898606i, complex arithmetic)
> complex i^i
i^i = exp(-pi/2)
  Re = exp(-pi/2),  Im = 0
  check: equal numerically (0.2078795764, complex arithmetic)
> complex (-1)^i
(-1)^i = exp(-pi)
  Re = exp(-pi),  Im = 0
  check: equal numerically (0.04321391826, complex arithmetic)
